  "question": {
    "text": "A combination of capacitors is set up as shown in the figure. The magnitude of the electric field, due to a point charge Q (having a charge equal to the sum of the charges on the <math><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&mu;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> and <math><mn>9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&mu;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> capacitors), at a point distant 30 m from it, would equal:<br />&nbsp; <img src=\"assets\\qt0133_9480157180e7.png\" style=\"width: 260px; height: 205px;\" />"
